  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02E7">Exercise <span data-tag="02E7">111.26.9</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field and let $A = k$ and $B = k[x, y]/(x^2, xy)$ with grading determined by $\deg (x) = 2$ and $\deg (y) = 3$. Let $\varphi (M) = \dim _ k(M)$. Compute the Hilbert function of $B$ as a graded $k$-module. Is there a Hilbert polynomial in this case? </p>
